Revision history for Perl distribution Lit

0.01  Unreleased
      - Initial version: portable lit and FileCheck in pure Perl.
      - Runs on OpenVMS (VAX, Alpha, I64, x86-64), Tru64 and Linux.
      - Internal shell (no /bin/sh required) with builtin commands.
      - dcl builtin: run verbatim DCL lines in one command procedure.
      - --output writes lit-format JSON results (last-run.json).
      - metrics builtin: record per-test values into the JSON results.
      - Verified on OpenVMS: the whole suite runs and passes there.
      - The shell lexer no longer splits a VMS file specification at the
        ';' introducing its version number.
      - Exit status decoding understands how Perl on OpenVMS maps exit(n)
        onto a condition value: exit(3) and exit(5) land on odd severities
        and previously read as success.
      - An unrecognised DCL verb now reports 127, as "command not found"
        does elsewhere.

      - MMS needs an explicit no-op on the degenerate subdirs-test_*
        targets MakeMaker emits; MMK does not care, MMS refuses.
      - Fixed on OpenVMS: VMS file specs are no longer read as glob
        patterns; a wrapper builtin no longer holds a write handle open
        across the command it wraps; the environment is applied as a
        delta rather than by replacing every logical name; subdirectories
        (NAME.DIR) are discovered; and scratch files land in SYS$SCRATCH:
        rather than [000000] on its volume.
